"""A programming-name boundary response, not a general parenthesis detector.

Calls, operators, subscripts and member/file suffixes get stronger responses
when they follow long ASCII identifiers. The preceding name's total length and its
last token fragment distinguish multi-token names from short math variables.
Snake_case and camelCase spelling provide small additional cues. Line endings
also get a boost immediately after a filename suffix. Blank lines after
reasoning tags receive small negative estimates. Other text stays near zero.
This is a fitted text heuristic; it does not identify every code context.
"""

