Uninterrupted token runs, long preceding fragments, path separators, and nearby
hyphens strengthen the response; preceding whitespace and capitals weaken it.
Bare hyphens and lowercase/uppercase suffixes have separately calibrated gains.
Initial hyphens are treated separately; hyphen/pipe-only runs are suppressed.
The next alphanumeric fragment gets a positive pulse. Whitespace after a word
suffix gets a small negative pulse. Otherwise output is zero. Clamp values to
[-0.6, 6.0] and reset all state at document boundaries.
