`var` is strongest at a document start or after @ in code annotations. TeX
commands and word-internal uses are weaker. Longer variable/change words,
war/window/server words, short v/r syllables, and selected multilingual forms
have smaller signals. Everything else is zero. Only the preceding character is
remembered, and that memory resets at document boundaries.
